---
import DarkLayout from "../layouts/DarkLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import ResonaraLogoFull from "../assets/ResonaraLogoFull.png";
import ResonaraSymbol from "../assets/ResonaraSymbol.png";
import ResonaraSymbol1 from "../assets/ResonaraSymbol1.png";
import ResonaraLusture from "../assets/ResonaraLusture.png";
---

<DarkLayout
  title="Resonara — The Story Behind the Symbol"
  description="The story behind the Resonara symbol — the mandala, the gear, the bowl, the mallet, the lock and the key."
>
  <!-- ═══════════ HERO ═══════════ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner fade-up">
      <div class="hero-eyebrow">The Mark</div>
      <div class="logo-plaque">
        <Image src={ResonaraLusture} alt="The Resonara logo — a mandala and gear enclosing a singing bowl and mallet, with the Resonara wordmark" width={900} quality={85} loading="eager" />
      </div>
      <h1 class="hero-title">The Story Behind the<br /><span>Resonara Symbol</span></h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="ornament"><span>✦</span></div>

  <!-- ═══════════ THE SYMBOL ═══════════ -->
  <section class="prose-section">
    <div class="prose-inner">
      <div class="fade-up">
        <span class="chapter-label">The Symbol</span>
      </div>
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">
          Every great idea deserves a mark. Not just a logo — a mark that holds meaning, that tells a story without words, that reveals itself to you slowly, the way wisdom does.
        </p>
        <p class="body-p">The Resonara symbol is one of those marks.</p>
        <p class="body-p">
          Look at it once and you see a beautiful emblem — a mandala, a mallet, a bowl. Look again, and something else emerges. Look a third time, and it tells you the whole story of what Resonara is.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════ THE BOWL AND THE MALLET ═══════════ -->
  <section class="prose-section dark-band">
    <div class="prose-inner">
      <div class="fade-up">
        <span class="chapter-eyebrow">What You See First</span>
        <h2 class="chapter-title">The Bowl and the <span>Mallet</span></h2>
      </div>

      <div class="symbol-feature fade-up">
        <Image src={ResonaraSymbol1} alt="The Resonara symbol — singing bowl and mallet held within a mandala and gear" width={520} quality={85} loading="lazy" />
      </div>

      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">At the centre of the symbol sits something ancient and elemental.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="statement fade-up">A mallet. A bowl.</p>
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">
          For thousands of years, across the Himalayas, across monasteries high in the mountains where silence is a practice and stillness is a discipline — monks have done this one simple thing: taken a
          mallet, touched it to a bowl, and let the sound arise.
        </p>
        <p class="body-p">
          That moment of contact is everything. The mallet meets the bowl, and what happens next cannot be manufactured or forced. The sound rises on its own. It radiates outward in concentric waves —
          visible to no one, felt by everyone. It moves through walls. It moves through the body. It moves through the noise in your mind and, for a moment, quiets it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="pull-quote fade-up">
        <p>This is where Resonara begins. That moment. That contact. That wave.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════ THE MANDALA AND THE GEAR ═══════════ -->
  <div class="ornament"><span>✦</span></div>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <div class="prose-inner">
      <div class="fade-up">
        <span class="chapter-eyebrow">What Holds It</span>
        <h2 class="chapter-title">The Mandala and the <span>Gear</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">Now look at what surrounds the mallet and bowl.</p>
        <p class="body-p">
          You'll see the petals of a mandala — the sacred geometry that Tibetan tradition has used for centuries to represent the universe in miniature. The mandala is a map. A map of order within
          complexity, of pattern within what seems like chaos. Every monk who created a sand mandala understood something profound: that the universe has structure, and when we align ourselves to that
          structure, we find peace.
        </p>
        <p class="body-p">But look more closely at the outer edge of the symbol. Those aren't just petals.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="statement fade-up">Those are the teeth of a gear.</p>
      <p class="statement statement--sub fade-up">Precise. Measured. Engineered to a tolerance.</p>
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">
          This is the other half of the Resonara story. The Tibetan singing bowl is one of the world's oldest instruments, but the machine that plays it — the Resonara device — is built with the
          precision of a Swiss watch. Every strike is calibrated. Every frequency is intentional. Every protocol has been designed with scientific rigour, so that what you receive is not random sound,
          but the exact vibration your nervous system needs.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="pull-quote fade-up">
        <p>Ancient wisdom. Modern precision. The mandala and the gear, held together in one symbol.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">
          This is the amalgamation that defines Resonara: the science and the sacred, the monastery and the laboratory, the soul and the stopwatch — each making the other more powerful.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════ THE LOCK AND THE KEY ═══════════ -->
  <section class="prose-section dark-band">
    <div class="prose-inner">
      <div class="fade-up">
        <span class="chapter-eyebrow">What You Don't See at First</span>
        <h2 class="chapter-title">The Lock and the <span>Key</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">Now step closer to the symbol. Look at the mallet and bowl again.</p>
        <p class="body-p">What else do you see?</p>
        <p class="body-p">The bowl — perfectly circular, perfectly enclosed. The mallet — upright, slender, precise.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="statement fade-up">A lock. And a key.</p>
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">
          This is the deeper story that the symbol holds, the one we didn't plan but that revealed itself to us the way truth often does — quietly, and only when you're ready to see it.
        </p>
        <p class="body-p">The Resonara machine is not just a sound bath device. It is a key.</p>
        <p class="body-p">
          The first door it opens is the one facing inward. Most of us live our entire lives as strangers to ourselves — reactive, restless, carrying a noise inside us that we've learned to drown out
          with more noise. The sound of the singing bowl cuts through all of that. It gives you access to a part of yourself you forgot existed. The lock is your own consciousness. The key is vibration.
        </p>
        <p class="body-p">
          The second door opens outward — into the universe itself. Every ancient tradition, from Vedic philosophy to quantum physics, points to the same truth: everything vibrates. The rock, the
          river, the star sixty thousand light years away — all of it is vibrating, resonating, participating in one vast conversation of frequency. The Resonara sound bath is your invitation to join
          that conversation. To stop being separate from it and remember that you never were.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="statement fade-up">The lock. The key. The self. The universe.</p>
      <p class="statement statement--italic fade-up">They were always the same thing.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════ THE NAME ═══════════ -->
  <div class="ornament"><span>✦</span></div>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <div class="prose-inner">
      <div class="fade-up">
        <span class="chapter-eyebrow">And the Name Itself</span>
        <h2 class="chapter-title">Reso<span>nara</span></h2>
      </div>
      <p class="statement fade-up">Resonara.</p>
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">The word itself is the teaching.</p>
        <p class="body-p">
          Resonance is what happens when one vibrating thing causes another to vibrate at the same frequency — not by force, but by invitation. It is the most natural phenomenon in physics, and the most
          profound metaphor in philosophy.
        </p>
        <p class="body-p">
          When you sit in a Resonara session, you resonate with the bowl. The bowl's frequency becomes yours. For a few moments, you are not fighting your own nature — you are aligned with it.
        </p>
        <p class="body-p">
          And when you sit in a group session, something else happens. People who have never met begin to breathe at the same pace. Their brainwaves begin to synchronise. Their nervous systems, which
          have been running at different rhythms all day, begin to move together. This is resonance between people — the ancient experience of sangha, of community, of the recognition that we are not
          isolated beings but interconnected ones.
        </p>
        <p class="body-p">And beyond that? Beyond the bowl, beyond the room, beyond the people around you?</p>
        <p class="body-p">We call these Humming Bowls. And there is a reason humming is the right word.</p>
        <p class="body-p">
          Think about the sound <em>mmm</em>. It is the most human sound there is. It is the sound you make in Bhramari pranayama — the ancient bee breath — when you close your lips and let vibration
          fill your skull, your chest, your entire being. It is the sound that escapes you when you are in pain — not a word, not a cry, just <em>mmm</em>, the body's oldest language. It is the sound you
          make when you learn something that suddenly makes sense, when insight lands and you don't yet have words for it. And it is the sound of deep ecstasy — of pleasure so complete that language
          dissolves into pure vibration.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="statement fade-up"><em>Mmm</em> is not a word. It is a state.</p>
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">
          The universe itself hums. It has been humming since before we had words for it — before we had words at all. The Vedic tradition called it Nada Brahma: the universe is sound. The humming bowl
          does not teach you something new. It reminds you of something you already know, in your cells, in your bones, in the oldest part of you that existed before thought. Resonara is simply an
          invitation to listen — and in listening, to remember that you and the universe are made of the same stuff, vibrating at the same note, part of the same one thing.
        </p>
        <p class="body-p">This is why the symbol is not just a logo.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="statement fade-up">It is a map. A key. A mandala. A machine.</p>
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">
          It is the whole story of Resonara — that the ancient and the modern are not opposites. That the self and the universe are not separate. That science and spirit are not in conflict.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="statement statement--italic fade-up">They are, like everything else, simply resonating.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════ CLOSING ═══════════ -->
  <div class="ornament"><span>✦</span></div>

  <section class="closing">
    <div class="closing-inner fade-up">
      <div class="closing-main">Resonara</div>
      <p class="closing-sub">Where Ancient Wisdom Meets Modern Precision</p>
      <a href="/story" class="cta-btn"><span>Read Our Story &nbsp;→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</DarkLayout>

<style>
  /* ── HERO ── */
  .hero {
    min-height: 70vh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
    padding: clamp(5rem, 12vw, 9rem) clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 2rem) 4rem;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, var(--dark) 0%, var(--dark-mid) 100%);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .hero::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center 42%, rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.08) 0%, transparent 68%);
  }
  .hero-inner {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  .hero-eyebrow {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(0.7rem, 1.8vw, 0.9rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.45em;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
  .logo-plaque {
    max-width: clamp(280px, 60vw, 440px);
    margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
    padding: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 1.8rem);
    border: 1px solid rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.28);
    background: rgba(250, 245, 233, 0.02);
    box-shadow:
      0 30px 70px -30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7),
      inset 0 0 60px rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.04);
    position: relative;
  }
  .logo-plaque::before,
  .logo-plaque::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--gold);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }
  .logo-plaque::before {
    top: 6px;
    left: 6px;
    border-right: none;
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  .logo-plaque::after {
    bottom: 6px;
    right: 6px;
    border-left: none;
    border-top: none;
  }
  .logo-plaque img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .hero-title {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--parchment);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .hero-title span {
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  /* ── PROSE ── */
  .prose-section {
    padding: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6.5rem) clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }
  .prose-inner {
    max-width: 740px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .dark-band {
    background: var(--dark-mid);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.1);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.1);
  }

  /* ── CHAPTER HEADINGS ── */
  .chapter-label {
    display: block;
    text-align: center;
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.6vw, 1.5rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .chapter-eyebrow {
    display: block;
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(0.7rem, 1.5vw, 0.85rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.34em;
    color: var(--gold);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.82;
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .chapter-title {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3.4vw, 2.3rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--parchment);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-bottom: 2.4rem;
  }
  .chapter-title span {
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  /* ── SYMBOL FEATURE IMAGE ── */
  .symbol-feature {
    max-width: clamp(220px, 45vw, 340px);
    margin: 0 auto 2.6rem;
    padding: clamp(0.8rem, 2.5vw, 1.4rem);
    border: 1px solid rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.22);
    background: rgba(250, 245, 233, 0.02);
    box-shadow: 0 24px 50px -28px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
  }
  .symbol-feature img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  /* ── STATEMENT LINES ── */
  .statement {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 3.2vw, 2rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--gold);
    text-align: center;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin: 2.2rem 0;
  }
  .statement--sub {
    font-size: clamp(0.95rem, 2vw, 1.25rem);
    color: var(--gold-pale);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    opacity: 0.85;
    margin-top: -0.8rem;
  }
  .statement--italic {
    font-family: "Cormorant Garamond", Georgia, serif;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--gold-pale);
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }
  .statement em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--gold-light);
  }

  /* ── CLOSING ── */
  .closing {
    text-align: center;
    padding: clamp(5rem, 11vw, 8rem) clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .closing::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.06) 0%, transparent 68%);
  }
  .closing-inner {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .closing-main {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--gold);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .closing-sub {
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.5vw, 1.5rem);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--gold-pale);
    opacity: 0.82;
    margin-bottom: 2.6rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* ── FADE-UP ── */
  .fade-up {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(28px);
    transition:
      opacity 0.75s ease,
      transform 0.75s ease;
  }
  .fade-up.visible {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
</style>

<script>
  const obs = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) =>
      entries.forEach((e) => {
        if (e.isIntersecting) {
          e.target.classList.add("visible");
          obs.unobserve(e.target);
        }
      }),
    { threshold: 0.08 },
  );
  document.querySelectorAll(".fade-up").forEach((el) => obs.observe(el));
</script>
